<item>
  <title>Daniela Arques, London City’s passing hub</title>
  <dc:creator>Federico Ninivaggi</dc:creator>
  <link>https://fniniv.github.io/blog/posts/2026-11-16-daniela-arques-london-city-s-passing-hub/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<style>:root{--tema:#2F6B3A;--tema-fg:#F4EEDF;--tema-acc:#F2C46B;--tema-ink:#2F6B3A;--tinta:#E6E8DA;}</style>
<header class="apertura column-screen" style="--fig-bg:#2F6B3A;--fig-fg:#F4EEDF;--fig-acc:#F2C46B"><div class="apertura-dentro"><div class="apertura-testo"><p class="testata-num">Nº 13 · football · Nov 16, 2026</p><h1 class="apertura-titolo">Daniela Arques, London City’s passing hub</h1><p class="apertura-sommario">Where she plays, how she passes and how she compares with the WSL’s central midfielders, in three graphics.</p><p class="tag-riga"><a class="tag-argomento" href="../../../en/blog.html#category=Football">Football</a></p><a class="testata-torna" href="../../../en/blog_calcio.html">↩ back to Football</a></div></div></header>

<p>Daniela Arques is London City’s passing hub: only two WSL central midfielders pass more often than her.</p>
<p>She builds through the middle from deep, then drifts left. In the two games she began on the bench, Grace Geyoro moved over to the left.</p>
<p><img src="https://fniniv.github.io/blog/posts/2026-11-16-daniela-arques-london-city-s-passing-hub/figura_1_dove.png" class="img-fluid" alt="Heat map of Daniela Arques's 690 touches for London City Lionesses, Women's Super League 2026/27, on a pitch with London City attacking upwards. The darkest areas are in her own half, in front of the defence, and on the left of the opponents' half. Text: Sits deep. 58% of her touches come in her own half, against 50% for a typical WSL holding midfielder; only 4 of the other 16 stay deeper."></p>
<p><img src="https://fniniv.github.io/blog/posts/2026-11-16-daniela-arques-london-city-s-passing-hub/figura_2_rotte.png" class="img-fluid" alt="Her 8 most-used passing routes as arrows on a pitch, London City attacking upwards. Her three signature routes, used at least 1.5 times as often as by a typical central midfielder, are highlighted on the left flank: two short passes along the left touchline in the opponents' half and a diagonal towards the wing. Text: Drifts left. In her own half she passes mostly through the middle; past halfway 42% of her passes start on the left, against 32% for a typical WSL central midfielder, and only 4 of the other 29 go left more often. In the 2 games she began on the bench, Grace Geyoro moved left: 68% of her passes started there, against 18% alongside Arques."></p>
<p><img src="https://fniniv.github.io/blog/posts/2026-11-16-daniela-arques-london-city-s-passing-hub/figura_3_confronto.png" class="img-fluid" alt="Ten measures comparing Daniela Arques with the 30 WSL central midfielders with at least 540 minutes, one dot per player; rank 1 is the highest value. On the ball: 3rd for touches and 3rd for passes per 90 minutes, 12th for pass accuracy, 6th for progressive passes, 20th for passes before a shot, 17th for long balls, 19th for touches in the opponents' half. Off the ball: 10th for balls won, 14th for how far up she wins the ball, 2nd of 11 for aerial duels won, 14 of 21. Text: London City's hub. Only 2 WSL central midfielders pass the ball more often; Grace Geyoro ranks 18th."></p>
<p><em>Women’s Super League 2026/27, matches up to 15 November 2026.</em></p>




<div class="firma-post">
<p>Federico Ninivaggi · November 16, 2026</p>
</div>

 ]]></description>
