<item>
  <title>Frida Maanum’s match against London City</title>
  <dc:creator>Federico Ninivaggi</dc:creator>
  <link>https://fniniv.github.io/blog/posts/2026-11-16-frida-maanum-s-match-against-london-city/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<style>:root{--tema:#2F6B3A;--tema-fg:#F4EEDF;--tema-acc:#F2C46B;--tema-ink:#2F6B3A;--tinta:#E6E8DA;}</style>
<header class="apertura column-screen" style="--fig-bg:#2F6B3A;--fig-fg:#F4EEDF;--fig-acc:#F2C46B"><div class="apertura-dentro"><div class="apertura-testo"><p class="testata-num">Nº 14 · football · Nov 16, 2026</p><h1 class="apertura-titolo">Frida Maanum’s match against London City</h1><p class="apertura-sommario">Her touches, passes, ball wins and shots in the 1-1 draw of 15 November 2026, on one graphic.</p><p class="tag-riga"><a class="tag-argomento" href="../../../en/blog.html#category=Football">Football</a></p><a class="testata-torna" href="../../../en/blog_calcio.html">↩ back to Football</a></div></div></header>

<p>First WSL start of the season for Frida Maanum, and all three of Arsenal’s big chances went through her: she scored the opener, set up a second and had the third saved at 1-1 in the 77th minute. In all she had a hand in 9 of Arsenal’s 17 shots.</p>
<p><img src="https://fniniv.github.io/blog/posts/2026-11-16-frida-maanum-s-match-against-london-city/figura.png" class="img-fluid" alt="Graphic titled Frida Maanum's match: Arsenal 1-1 London City, Women's Super League. Stat line: 98 minutes, 49 touches, 22 of 31 passes completed, 7 progressive passes, 4 key passes, 5 shots with 1 goal, 5 ball wins. A heat map shows 67% of her touches in the opponent's half and 47% on the left third of the pitch. A pass map shows her passes, with progressive passes in blue and key passes in red. A pitch shows her 5 ball wins, 3 of them in her own half. A shot map shows 4 of her 5 shots taken inside the box, including the goal in the 10th minute."></p>
<p><strong>How to read it.</strong> A big chance is a clear scoring chance. A key pass is the pass before a teammate’s shot. A progressive pass is completed, gains at least a tenth of the pitch and cuts the distance to the goal line by at least a quarter. The heat map blurs each of her 49 touches over about 14 metres. Ball wins are balls won back by recoveries, interceptions or tackles, counted once per ball.</p>
<p><em>Women’s Super League 2026/27.</em></p>




<div class="firma-post">
<p>Federico Ninivaggi · November 16, 2026</p>
</div>

 ]]></description>
